# Rust
/target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.pdb

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tauri
# (build output lands in the workspace-root /target/ above, not
# src-tauri/target/ -- this is a Cargo workspace, not a standalone crate;
# confirmed the hard way when ci.yml's installer-upload step looked in the
# wrong place and silently uploaded nothing, see ci.yml's comment)
/gen/
# tauri-build's codegen output (schemas/capabilities), regenerated on every
# build. The root-anchored `/gen/` above only covers a standalone-crate
# layout; in this workspace the real directory is src-tauri/gen, which was
# showing up as untracked until it was ignored explicitly here.
/src-tauri/gen/

# the frontend build consumes it. Never hand-edit; never commit -- keeping
# it generated-only avoids a hand-transcribed copy silently drifting from
# the real Rust command signatures.

# Cargo.lock is committed at the workspace root (reproducible builds,
# master plan S4.1) but Rust crates without a [[bin]]/cdylib target do not
# need their own; only the root one matters here since this is a single
# workspace, not independently published crates.

# Environment / secrets — never committed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/icons/*.key

# Provider CLI credential/session directories — must never enter a public repo
.claude/
.codex/
.copilot/
.gemini/
.opencode/
.antigravity/
**/*.credentials.json
**/auth.json

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.log
logs/

# NACC local runtime state
.nacc-worktrees/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal

# Local scratch / tooling output -- never part of the repository
.freebuff/
output/
